we begin with a very terrible story it  involves a plane crash in Africa  Ethiopian Airlines is now grounded the  rest of its brand-new Boeing 737 max  eight Jets while it investigates  Sunday's crash that killed 157 people  flight 302 tuner OB Kenya went down  minutes after takeoff from Ethiopia  Ethiopia's capital addis ababa the  victims came from 35 different countries  and eight of them are American the  planes black boxes have been found but  the cause of the crash is still unknown  it's the second accident in five months  involving a Boeing Max 8 jet  Debora patta is in is at Jomo Kenyatta  International Airport in Nairobi where  the plane was supposed to land  good morning many of the people aboard  Ethiopian Airlines flight 302 were  heading here to Nairobi to attend the  United Nations conference the US has  sent its condolences to all the families  of those on board the plane piles of  mangled debris lie scattered around the  crash site strewn amongst the wreckage  items of clothing and personal  belongings a jarring reminder of just  how many lives were lost  the arrival board simply read flight  delayed at Nairobi's International  Airport yesterday while back in Ethiopia  reality began to sink in for frantic  relatives after the news was announced  the Ethiopian Airlines CEO faced the  public we are very very saddened flight  302 took off at 838 local time from  Ethiopia's Bolle International Airport  in Addis Ababa heading for Nairobi  seconds later the pilot made a distress  call wanting to turn back then of just  six minutes into the flight all contact  was lost and the plane crashed in debris  site 31 miles south of the capital an  eyewitness described seeing the plane go  down  it came directly from the sky downwards  he said and we heard a huge explosion  the jet was a new Boeing 737 max eight  that the airline had recently purchased  at the end of last year on the plane  35 nationalities from around the world  so many of those people had dedicated  their lives to helping others the United  Nations has been hard hit by the crash  losing 19 staff members from people  providing safety for Refugees to those  fighting world hunger the flight  manifest reads like a list of the very  best of humanity the CBS this morning  Debora patta Nairobi Kenya  such a terrible story
 

